From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9umd: nine's texture memory when the host says none

A host GL without a way to say how much video memory it has (no GL_NVX_gpu_memory_info, ATI_meminfo or
MESA_query_renderer: older GPUs, and llvmpipe with 2010's extensions) gives PIPE_CAP_VIDEO_MEMORY 0, and gallium
nine's texture memory counter then refused every resource with D3DERR_OUTOFVIDEOMEMORY: no Direct3D 9 device
could be made. Then nine counts from 4 GB (override_vram_size); the kernel driver holds the real limit.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d9umd/nine_bridge.c b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d9umd/nine_bridge.c
index af05dfd..30a5425 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d9umd/nine_bridge.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d9umd/nine_bridge.c
@@ -113,7 +113,11 @@ nddi_init_context(struct d3dadapter9_context *ctx, struct pipe_screen *screen)
    /* The DDI calls arrive serialized from the runtime; no worker thread */
    ctx->csmt_force = 0;
    ctx->memfd_virtualsizelimit = -1;
-   ctx->override_vram_size = -1;
+   /* A host that doesn't say how much video memory it has (no GL_NVX_gpu_memory_info, ATI_meminfo or
+    * MESA_query_renderer: older GPUs) reports 0, and nine's texture memory counter then refused every resource
+    * (D3DERR_OUTOFVIDEOMEMORY: no Direct3D 9 device at all). Then 4 GB: the counter is nine's own, the kernel driver
+    * holds the real limit (GpuMemoryLimitMB) */
+   ctx->override_vram_size = screen->get_param(screen, PIPE_CAP_VIDEO_MEMORY) ? -1 : 4096;
 }
 
 /* ---- Adapter ---- */
